MID_EV14_010_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV14_010_m01_001: I'm back. It appears we haven't been followed.
MID_EV14_010_m01_002: I have news too. The tavern proprietress informed\nme our faces have turned up on wanted posters.
MID_EV14_010_m01_003: Seems we're wanted by Arago for not only Balboa's\nmurder but for masterminding the Cydonia rebellion.
MID_EV14_010_m01_004: Alas, they did an awful job capturing my likeness.\nI am far more handsome than depicted.
MID_EV14_010_m01_005: I'm sorry, but how long are you two planning to\nfollow me around?
MID_EV14_010_m01_006: I mean, I ran away and went on this whole journey\nso I could find my mom...
MID_EV14_010_m01_007: But you saved my life, and I want to pay you back.\nGuess I thought I'd stick around until I could do that.
MID_EV14_010_m01_008: Don't be ridiculous. I didn't kill Bjor to save you.\nI killed him because that was my plan. Understand?
MID_EV14_010_m01_009: Well, I find you all entirely fascinating. So I'll be\nsticking around to see how this plays out.
MID_EV14_010_m01_010: You know the saying "Curiosity killed the cat"? You\nare dangerous-close to being the cat here.
MID_EV14_010_m01_011: You do realize we're on wanted posters now. There's\nno turning back—not for Mu and not for me.
MID_EV14_010_m01_012: I know another saying. It goes, "We're all in the same\nboat." So you might try thinking of us as allies.
MID_EV14_010_m01_013: Also, don't you think it's about time the two of you\ntold us who you are?
MID_EV14_010_m01_014: Fine. Why not?
MID_EV14_010_m01_015: Milady... Are you sure?
MID_EV14_010_m01_016: We used to live in Cydonia. We were there when\nthe invasion began...
MID_EV14_010_m01_017: I admit this is quite a surprise. You're the daughter\nof the deposed viceroy of Cydonia...
MID_EV14_010_m01_018: Which means...you must be Leilidahna.
MID_EV14_010_m01_019: If you know who she is, then I have a good idea who\nyou work for.
MID_EV14_010_m01_020: She's famous—the youngest person ever to win the\nRose of Caelus title at the temple of Kalla.
MID_EV14_010_m01_021: I'd heard that you died during the Cydonia Massacre.\nThey said you burned in the flames.
MID_EV14_010_m01_022: But here you are. Kalla would be overjoyed to hear\nthis news.
MID_EV14_010_m01_023: I'm a wanted criminal now. I could never present\nmyself before the goddess like this.
MID_EV14_010_m01_024: You certainly could. She has missed you dearly and\nfor far too long.
MID_EV14_010_m01_025: *sigh*
MID_EV14_010_m01_026: After what happened, Buccar and I escaped to the\ncounty of Ortill in the kingdom of Arago.
MID_EV14_010_m01_027: Father Mahdel took us in and protected us. He was\nin charge of one of the Dagda temple shrines there.
MID_EV14_010_m01_028: If memory serves, Father Mahdel was a high priest\nin Dagda's temple.
MID_EV14_010_m01_029: I'd heard he went into hiding after he was accused\nof some kind of scandal.
MID_EV14_010_m01_030: Yes, that's him. He was my father's best friend,\nfrom the days they lived in Dagsion.
MID_EV14_010_m01_031: I spent my time there trying to stay hidden\nand training with Buccar.
MID_EV14_010_m01_032: Only one thing kept me going—the thought of killing\nGeneral Bertrand, the man who murdered my father.
MID_EV14_010_m01_033: Then one day I snuck into Grand Aragon, the capital\nof Arago. I didn't tell Father Mahdel.
MID_EV14_010_m01_034: What I discovered there nearly destroyed me.\nBertrand was already dead—executed for treason.
MID_EV14_010_m01_035: It was like the whole world fell out from under my\nfeet. Killing that man had been everything to me.
MID_EV14_010_m01_036: After that, I had no reason to live. I just felt\nso hollow.
MID_EV14_010_m01_037: That's when Father Mahdel began hinting that\nCydonia had been swept up into larger conspiracies.
MID_EV14_010_m01_038: He promised to reveal the secrets he knew as soon as\nI was strong enough to do something about them.
MID_EV14_010_m01_039: And then, somehow, three years passed...
MID_EV14_011_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV14_011_m01_001: You've grown so much stronger over these past\nyears, Leilidahna.
MID_EV14_011_m01_002: It's time I give you this. You'll have to decide what\nyou do...once you understand what I've written there.
MID_EV14_011_m01_003: Father Mahdel...what is this?
MID_EV14_011_m01_004: It is a detailed list of names and crimes. These are\nthe people who deserve your vengeance.
MID_EV14_011_m01_005: This is...what you told me about years ago?
MID_EV14_011_m01_006: It is. These are the secrets I promised to you then.
MID_EV14_011_m01_007: I've recorded all I know about the conspiracies\nsurrounding the Cydonia Massacre.
MID_EV14_011_m01_008: *gasp*
MID_EV14_011_m01_009: Father Mahdel, I...I don't understand...
MID_EV14_011_m01_010: Why is your name at the top of this list?!
MID_EV14_011_m01_011: I testified before the Divine Sovereign using false\nevidence given to me by the people on that list.
MID_EV14_011_m01_012: My testimony painted Guillermo as corrupt and\ntreasonous. It undermined your father severely.
MID_EV14_011_m01_013: And that evidence I presented...it was the excuse\nthey needed to make a move on Cydonia.
MID_EV14_011_m01_014: A-ah... Father Mahdel...what are you...
MID_EV14_011_m01_015: If you believe nothing else, Leilidahna, you must\nbelieve this...
MID_EV14_011_m01_016: I never wanted any of that to happen. Your father...\nI did not intend for him to...
MID_EV14_011_m01_017: They had taken my family hostage, you see. I had no\nchoice but to do what they demanded.
MID_EV14_011_m01_018: But in doing so, I betrayed my best friend.
MID_EV14_011_m01_019: You, of all people... How could you?
MID_EV14_011_m01_020: Do you have any idea how much my father\ntrusted you?
MID_EV14_011_m01_021: I would never ask you to understand.
MID_EV14_011_m01_022: But please believe me when I say I've been wracked\nby guilt day and night ever since.
MID_EV14_011_m01_023: So I am revealing the truth to you and entrusting\nyou with this list...
MID_EV14_011_m01_024: In this way, I hope to atone for these sins against\nmy dear friend Guillermo.
MID_EV14_011_m01_025: Now, you have my confession and my list. At last,\nI can take responsibility for what I've done.
MID_EV14_011_m01_026: Father Mahdel, what do you mean?!
MID_EV14_011_m01_027: What...what have you done?
MID_EV14_011_m01_028: Flames will soon engulf this place. You must go now.
MID_EV14_011_m01_029: Why? Why are you doing this?!
MID_EV14_011_m01_030: I will not move from here. This is where we\nsay goodbye, Leilidahna.
MID_EV14_011_m01_031: I pray that you find happiness in this life.
MID_EV14_011_m01_032: Milady, we can't stay here! We must go! Hurry!
MID_EV14_011_m01_033: Father Mahdel!
MID_EV14_012_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV14_012_m01_001: *sniffle*
MID_EV14_012_m01_002: I see. I had no idea.
MID_EV14_012_m01_003: When the fire finally died, we found his corpse in the\nashes, burnt beyond recognition.
MID_EV14_012_m01_004: Father Mahdel had left me his list. So, I set out to\ntake my revenge on those he had named.
MID_EV14_012_m01_005: The "Mahdel List," is it? You do realize that man is\nguilty of some truly unforgivable sins.
MID_EV14_012_m01_006: Indeed. He never should have brought those lies\nbefore the Divine Sovereign...
MID_EV14_012_m01_007: That's not the sin I mean. I'm talking about that list\nhe gave to Miss Leda.
MID_EV14_012_m01_008: You see, if it's true that Balboa's faction was plotting\nto seize Cydonia...
MID_EV14_012_m01_009: they would have found a way to carry out their plan,\nwith or without Father Mahdel's testimony.
MID_EV14_012_m01_010: If he'd failed to do what they wanted, they'd simply\nhave found someone else to do their bidding.
MID_EV14_012_m01_011: One way or another, they'd have made sure the\nCydonia Massacre happened.
MID_EV14_012_m01_012: My point is I can't help but wonder if Miss Leda\nwould've been better off not knowing about any of it.
MID_EV14_012_m01_013: Hm. You might be right about that.
MID_EV14_012_m01_014: I can't forgive Father Mahdel for everything he's\ndone, but I am grateful to him.
MID_EV14_012_m01_015: This list has kept me going. It's given me a reason\nto live.
MID_EV14_012_m01_016: I find it strange that in all that time, I never heard\neven a whisper that you survived.
MID_EV14_012_m01_017: If it's because the father had you hidden at his\nshrine...I suppose that makes sense.
MID_EV14_012_m01_018: And now that I know who you are, that must mean\nthe vihuela with you is Obsidian.
MID_EV14_012_m01_019: It's the instrument once owned by Cohen himself...\nthe self-proclaimed "legendary bard."
MID_EV14_012_m01_020: Yes, House Cohendia has safeguarded it for\ngenerations—ever since his death.
MID_EV14_012_m01_021: When Kassite burned, it was the only thing\nI was able to bring with me.
MID_EV14_012_m01_022: Um, I've been thinking... I still want to help\nyou, Leda.
MID_EV14_012_m01_023: I mean, I want to repay you for saving me...
MID_EV14_012_m01_024: but also, if anyone ever did anything to my mom,\nI'd hate them too.
MID_EV14_012_m01_025: And I want to help you because I...I like you.
MID_EV14_012_m01_026: Uh, OK... What a strange thing to say.
MID_EV14_012_m01_027: But I mean it! I do.
MID_EV14_012_m01_028: There's nothing strange about it. Affection can arise\nas suddenly and unexpectedly as a gust of wind.
MID_EV14_012_m01_029: Now, since Miss Leda shared her secret with us, it\nonly seems fair that I reveal my identity as well.
MID_EV14_012_m01_030: Sirocco is my alias. My true name is Syracusio.
MID_EV14_012_m01_031: I am a vulkan serving Kalla's temple. My vulkan\nname is Syracusio of the Silver Hail.
MID_EV14_012_m01_032: I have been secretly conducting an investigation into\nthe kingdom of Arago at the goddess Kalla's behest.
MID_EV14_012_m01_033: There it is. Just as I thought.
MID_EV14_012_m01_034: Miss Leda, allow me to make clear my promise. You\nhave my full cooperation. I am here to help you.
MID_EV14_012_m01_035: Can a temple vulkan really afford to help\na murderer?
MID_EV14_012_m01_036: Please understand, my lady Kalla cares for you\nvery much.
MID_EV14_012_m01_037: I can assure you that my actions from here on are in\nconcert with her wishes.
MID_EV14_012_m01_038: I appreciate that, but...I feel like we've hit a dead\nend when it comes to Lechner.
MID_EV14_012_m01_039: It's true—we didn't get even a scrap of information\nout of Balboa.
MID_EV14_012_m01_040: Balboa set a trap at the bottom of the mine and was\nlying in wait for you.
MID_EV14_012_m01_041: Does that mean Balboa had an, uh, accomplice\nmaybe? Someone who was watching us?
MID_EV14_012_m01_042: That's exactly what it means, Mu. Very good.\nYou catch on quickly.
MID_EV14_012_m01_043: Let's not forget the wanted posters. It's going to be\ndifficult to move about freely from now on.
MID_EV14_012_m01_044: Miss Leda, if you don't mind my asking, what do you\nthink of heading to Kalla's temple for a spell?
MID_EV14_012_m01_045: I really do think you should meet with my lady.\nI'm certain she'll offer us some assistance.
MID_EV14_012_m01_046: Ahh.
MID_EV14_013_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV14_013_m01_001: If we're stopping here, am I correct in assuming Miss\nLeda plans to pay her respects to her ancestor?
MID_EV14_013_m01_002: You could say that.
MID_EV14_013_m01_003: What is this place? Those look like old gravestones.
MID_EV14_013_m01_004: It's called Cohen's Mausoleum. The legendary bard\nCohen is buried here.
MID_EV14_013_m01_005: The grieving goddess Kalla built this place after\nhis death.
MID_EV14_013_m01_006: So that means one of Leda's old family members\nis buried here?
MID_EV14_013_m01_007: <NCA>Explain the history for Mu.
MID_EV14_013_m01_008: Cohen was a renowned bard who lived about\nfive hundred years ago.
MID_EV14_013_m01_009: They say he proved to be a singing and performing\nprodigy at a very young age.
MID_EV14_013_m01_010: But they also say that in his later years, he lost\nhis mind and met with a rather tragic end.
MID_EV14_013_m01_011: Oh no!
MID_EV14_013_m01_012: More importantly, perhaps...Miss Leda's Obsidian\nis the same instrument that Cohen himself played.
MID_EV14_013_m01_013: Miss Leda, this is just a hunch, but isn't Obsidian\nalso one of Drake's treasures?
MID_EV14_013_m01_014: While these treasures give power to their owners,\nit's said they also eat away at their spirit.
MID_EV14_013_m01_015: <NCA>Talk about Obsidian's power.
MID_EV14_013_m01_016: <NCB>Mention what happened with Balboa.
MID_EV14_013_m01_017: <ACA>I admit I do feel a strange power coming\nfrom Obsidian sometimes.
MID_EV14_013_m01_018: <ACA>When I get ready to play my vihuela, I hear a voice\nwhisper to me. It says, "Strum your soul."
MID_EV14_013_m01_019: <ACA>Every time I hear it, I— I wonder whose voice\nthat is.
MID_EV14_013_m01_020: <ACB>When Balboa revealed her treasure, Obsidian seemed\nto...resonate with it.
MID_EV14_013_m01_021: <ACB>I'd never felt anything like it before. So, yeah,\nmaybe Obsidian is what you say it is.
MID_EV14_013_m01_022: If that's true and you keep Obsidian in your\npossession...you'll end up like Cohen one day.
MID_EV14_013_m01_023: Maybe. But right now I need Obsidian's power.
MID_EV14_013_m01_024: Hey...do you hear that? It sounds like someone's\nplaying a vihuela.
MID_EV14_013_m01_025: It does. And they sound like a highly skilled player\nat that.
MID_EV14_013_m01_026: I didn't think there was another vihuela player who\ncould match your talent, Miss Leda.
MID_EV14_013_m01_027: I can't hear anything. Ugh. Young people and their\ngood hearing.
MID_EV14_013_m01_028: Eeyaaah!
MID_EV14_013_m01_029: I heard that! Sounded like a woman screaming.
MID_EV14_013_m01_030: Could be bandits attacking a traveler.
MID_EV14_013_m01_031: We can't just ignore it. We have to help.
MID_EV14_013_m01_032: Miss Leda! We're being hunted too, you know.\nIgnoring it might be our best option.
MID_EV14_013_m01_033: Please. I'm not so far down the road to ruin that I'm\nwilling to turn my back on someone who needs help.
MID_EV14_013_m01_034: I know I can be cold and maybe even a little\nabrasive. But I'm not THAT unfeeling.
MID_EV14_013_m01_035: W-wait for me, Leda! I'm coming with you!
MID_EV14_013_m01_036: How very unexpected. I was sure she'd have no\ninterest in someone else's needs.
MID_EV14_013_m01_037: Despite what you think, she has a kind heart. Milady\ndoesn't want anyone to go through what she did.
MID_EV14_013_m01_038: She's a passionate woman, more so than I gave her\ncredit for. I confess it only adds to her charm.
MID_EV14_014_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV14_014_m01_001: You saved my life. How can I thank you?
MID_EV14_014_m01_002: My name is Maria, by the way. It seems we're in the\nsame line of work. I'm a bard too, you see.
MID_EV14_014_m01_003: It's dangerous for a woman to travel alone. Why don't\nI send this loudmouth with you for protection?
MID_EV14_014_m01_004: Me? A loudmouth? Hahaha. I do enjoy our breezy\nbanter, Miss Leda.
MID_EV14_014_m01_005: Oh, you're a loudmouth alright...among other things.
MID_EV14_014_m01_006: I don't get it. What is someone like you doing in this\nsort of place?
MID_EV14_014_m01_007: A musician like me can't possibly ignore the allure of\nthe legendary bard's resting place.
MID_EV14_014_m01_008: I always stop to pay my respects when I pass through\nhere. Though I was caught quite off guard today.
MID_EV14_014_m01_009: Well, I'm glad you're OK.
MID_EV14_014_m01_010: Oh...what is that scent? It's sooo pretty. It smells like\nshe came from the heavens.
MID_EV14_014_m01_011: What is it, Mu? You seem lost in thought. Ah, hmm...\nI understand now.
MID_EV14_014_m01_012: That is a lovely fragrance you're wearing, Maria.\nIt suits you very well.
MID_EV14_014_m01_013: Heehee. I'm so glad you like it.
MID_EV14_014_m01_014: Her fragrance... It's ambergris from the southern sea.\nGood quality too. She pretends she's no one special...
MID_EV14_014_m01_015: but ambergris is rare enough that she'd have to be\nroyalty, nobility, or a goddess to wear it so casually.
MID_EV14_014_m01_016: I also hear that it's used in aphrodisiacs. This beauty\nmight just be some kind of enchantress.
MID_EV14_014_m01_017: You don't wear perfume, Sirocco. So how come you\nknow so much about it?
MID_EV14_014_m01_018: This knowledge is easy to come by...when one spends\nas many nights with as many beauties as I do.
MID_EV14_014_m01_019: Blech! Sirocco, you're disgusting! Just— Just stay\naway from me!
MID_EV14_014_m01_020: <NCA>Comment on Maria's instrument.
MID_EV14_014_m01_021: There's something unusual about your vihuela,\nisn't there?
MID_EV14_014_m01_022: I noticed it earlier too...
MID_EV14_014_m01_023: It gives off this...feeling...that reminds me of my\nvihuela. Obsidian—that's the name of my instrument.
MID_EV14_014_m01_024: Mine is called Moonstone, and it's the vihuela that\nonce belonged to the Virtuosa of Heaven and Earth.
MID_EV14_014_m01_025: Virtuosa of Heaven and Earth... I've never heard\nthat name before. Who's that?
MID_EV14_014_m01_026: Hmm, well...they say she lived around the\nsame time that Cohen did.
MID_EV14_014_m01_027: Not much is known about her except that she was\nan extraordinary musician.
MID_EV14_014_m01_028: It's said her music seemed to rain down from heaven.\nAnd when she sang, the earth trembled with joy.
MID_EV14_014_m01_029: It's also said she played a pair of vihuelas—one that\nrepresented the heavens and one the earth.
MID_EV14_014_m01_030: I wonder... What if Cohen met this Virtuosa of\nHeaven and Earth during his travels...
MID_EV14_014_m01_031: and while they spent time together, she entrusted\nObsidian to him?
MID_EV14_014_m01_032: If that's true, then it would mean your Obsidian...
MID_EV14_014_m01_033: is the long-lost sister to this heavenly vihuela\nof mine.
MID_EV14_014_m01_034: Tell me—where are you all going next?
MID_EV14_014_m01_035: <NCA>Answer her question.
MID_EV14_014_m01_036: We're headed to Kalla's temple.
MID_EV14_014_m01_037: Ah, then we're traveling in the same direction.\nPerhaps I'll join you, if you don't mind.
MID_EV14_014_m01_038: Someone as lovely as yourself is welcome anytime.\nMiss Leda and I will do our best to protect you.
MID_EV14_014_m01_039: Bleh! Do you hear yourself? You JUST said we\nshould leave her to the bandits or whatever.
MID_EV14_014_m01_040: Seriously, Sirocco, you are so obnoxious.
MID_EV14_014_m01_041: I concur.
MID_EV14_015_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV14_015_m01_001: Lo, my lady, it is I, Syracusio. Your faithful knight\nhas, at long last, returned.
MID_EV14_015_m01_002: Oh, how these many days your servant has longed to\nlay eyes upon you and bathe in thy sorrowful gaze.
MID_EV14_015_m01_003: Ah, you've arrived just in time. There was no one left\nwith a whit of skill to play my board games with.
MID_EV14_015_m01_004: To atone for the lengthy period of loneliness I forced\nupon you, I shall stay with you as long as you desire...
MID_EV14_015_m01_005: Through the night, if need be...and in your bedroom,\nif you wish.
MID_EV14_015_m01_006: I'm relieved to see that your travels have not\ndampened your sense of humor.
MID_EV14_015_m01_007: Now tell me—you have returned earlier than\nplanned. Did something happen?
MID_EV14_015_m01_008: I've returned with information about a certain tragic\nevent...and with people you will be pleased to see.
MID_EV14_015_m01_009: My goodness... Leilidahna? You're alive?!
MID_EV14_015_m01_010: <NCA>Greet her.
MID_EV14_015_m01_011: It's been too long, Kalla. I'm so glad to see that\nyou're well.
MID_EV14_015_m01_012: And I apologize for neglecting my duties to you for\nsuch a long time. I know I owe you a great debt.
MID_EV14_015_m01_013: After what happened in Cydonia, I sent so very\nmany people to look for you...
MID_EV14_015_m01_014: None of them could find you, and they returned with\nsuch grim reports. I feared you...had not survived.
MID_EV14_015_m01_015: You did survive, and here you are. And I am\noverjoyed you made your way back to me.
MID_EV14_015_m01_016: I'm so sorry. I found Father Mahdel and went\ninto hiding.
MID_EV14_015_m01_017: This is so amazing. Leda knows the goddess?
MID_EV14_015_m01_018: Lady Leda came to Kalla's temple to train in the arts\nwhen she was just 10 years old.
MID_EV14_015_m01_019: When she was 13, she became the youngest person\nto win the title Rose of Caelus.
MID_EV14_015_m01_020: Is being the Rose of Caelus a big deal or something?
MID_EV14_015_m01_021: It is. The title is given only to those who earn special\nrecognition from the goddess Kalla herself.
MID_EV14_015_m01_022: It usually goes to the winner of the Rose\nPageant held at Kalla's temple every year...
MID_EV14_015_m01_023: Leda's win caused quite a to-do at the time. It was\nunheard of for someone so young to earn the title.
MID_EV14_015_m01_024: Sadly, I was away from the temple on a mission, so\nI wasn't here to see it unfold for myself.
MID_EV14_015_m01_025: Leilidahna, it has been so long since I last heard you\nplay the vihuela. Do you mind?
MID_EV14_015_m01_026: Not at all. It would be my honor to play for you.
MID_EV14_016_m01_001: Wonderful. Truly. Your skills have improved greatly.\nHowever...
MID_EV14_016_m01_002: I sense an unusual presence coming from that\nvihuela. Leilidahna, tell me—is it...
MID_EV14_016_m01_003: Yes, it's Cohen's instrument. This heirloom from my\nancestor has been in my family for many generations.
MID_EV14_016_m01_004: The inscription says it's called Obsidian. It was the\nonly thing I escaped with when Cydonia burned.
MID_EV14_016_m01_005: I've heard the stories, but this is the first time I've\nhad a chance to lay eyes upon it in person.
MID_EV14_016_m01_006: Leilidahna, may I take a closer look at your vihuela?
MID_EV14_016_m01_007: <NCA>Show Obsidian to her.
MID_EV14_016_m01_008: How deeply, profoundly ominous it is. And yet, still\nits beauty surpasses its darkness.
MID_EV14_016_m01_009: Leilidahna, don't you think it best to use this\ninstrument as sparingly as possible?
MID_EV14_016_m01_010: It is known to bring disaster upon the musician who\nplays it. Surely you've heard how Cohen met his end.
MID_EV14_016_m01_011: No... I haven't really heard the story in much detail.
MID_EV14_016_m01_012: In his later years, Cohen spent his days convalescing\nat the home of a local noble named Brachi Dia.
MID_EV14_016_m01_013: Cohen was emaciated by that time and would often\njust stare vacantly and mutter to himself.
MID_EV14_016_m01_014: Brachi Dia's daughter, Valencia, dedicated herself to\nhis care, and he briefly showed signs of recovering...
MID_EV14_016_m01_015: But then one day, Cohen went mad. He ran from\nthe house screaming...
MID_EV14_016_m01_016: He ran straight to the cape and jumped into the sea.\nAnd he never returned.
MID_EV14_016_m01_017: I...didn't know that's what happened to him.
MID_EV14_016_m01_018: Ah yes, it's a tragic tale. He was a prodigious talent\nand a legendary bard...
MID_EV14_016_m01_019: The speculation surrounding his death remains a\nfavorite subject among performers to this day.
MID_EV14_016_m01_020: When Cohen died, Valencia was pregnant with\nhis child.
MID_EV14_016_m01_021: Thereupon, my dear goddess Kalla bestowed upon\nBrachi Dia a new family name—Cohendia.
MID_EV14_016_m01_022: And so it became the name of your house,\nMiss Leda.
MID_EV14_016_m01_023: I appreciate you worrying over my well-being, Kalla.\nIt's more than I deserve.
MID_EV14_016_m01_024: But Obsidian has a power that I need right now.
MID_EV14_016_m01_025: I don't understand, Leilidahna. What do you mean?
MID_EV14_016_m01_026: I mean the Cydonia Massacre took every good thing\nI ever had away from me.
MID_EV14_016_m01_027: The only thing that's kept me going since then is\nmy hatred for the people who are responsible.
MID_EV14_016_m01_028: Ah, Leilidahna...someone so young should not have\nto walk a path so full of carnage and strife.
MID_EV14_016_m01_029: Please, can't you leave the past behind and find\nhappiness for yourself instead?
MID_EV14_016_m01_030: I don't know what happiness feels like anymore.\nAnd I don't care. Revenge is all that matters now.
MID_EV14_016_m01_031: Take that away from me, and I... I'm prepared to\ntake my own life.
MID_EV14_016_m01_032: Leilidahna, no...
MID_EV14_016_m01_033: Leilidahna, I knew it! I knew that if anyone was\ngoing to survive that awful tragedy, it was you!
MID_EV14_016_m01_034: Wait...Olympia?
MID_EV14_016_m01_035: Wow, who is that? She's...incredible!
MID_EV14_016_m01_036: Her name is Olympia, and she is a priest. Like Miss\nLeda, she too was granted the title Rose of Caelus.
MID_EV14_016_m01_037: I am simply overjoyed that you remember me! Why,\nI don't know what I'd have done if you had not!
MID_EV14_016_m01_038: Well, truth be told, I'd have been quite put out! After\nall, you are the only opponent to sully my name.
MID_EV14_016_m01_039: Olympia, I never meant to—
MID_EV14_016_m01_040: Someone TWO years my junior stole the title right\nout from under me at the Rose Pageant that year.
MID_EV14_016_m01_041: After that, I challenged you to one battle of skill after\nanother... And oh, the tears I cried with every loss!
MID_EV14_016_m01_042: Eventually you left the temple, as though you'd\nsimply decided to quit while you were ahead.
MID_EV14_016_m01_043: I DID finally earn the title Blue Rose of Caelus. Still,\nI have continued my studies and bided my time...
MID_EV14_016_m01_044: And now, Leilidahna, my time has come! I will settle\nthe score and show you which of us is the true Rose!
MID_EV14_017_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV14_017_m01_001: I can't believe I lost. And so...so BADLY. Me!
MID_EV14_017_m01_002: I don't know about that. I felt like I won by a hair's\nbreadth. It wasn't a bad match.
MID_EV14_017_m01_003: Oh! That's right.
MID_EV14_017_m01_004: The only reason I even lost...is because of the power\nin that vihuela of yours!
MID_EV14_017_m01_005: No way! She lost, and she wants to blame it on\nan instrument?!
MID_EV14_017_m01_006: Give it to me, and I'll show you that I can play it far\nbetter than you could ever hope to!
MID_EV14_017_m01_007: Now then, listen carefully, everyone.
MID_EV14_017_m01_008: Hm?
MID_EV14_017_m01_009: Wh-what's wrong with this thing? Is it broken\nor something?!
MID_EV14_017_m01_010: Olympia is playing her hardest, but it's not making\na sound.
MID_EV14_017_m01_011: Even this instrument looks down upon me!\nOh, the humiliation! *SOB*
MID_EV14_017_m01_012: <NCA>Comfort her.
MID_EV14_017_m01_013: <NCB>Leave her be.
MID_EV14_017_m01_048: <ACB>
MID_EV14_017_m01_014: <ACA>No tears, OK? It's not your fault. You just have to\nbe...compatible...with an instrument. That's all.
MID_EV14_017_m01_015: <ACA>But this vihuela clearly doesn't like me! I can tell!\nEVERYONE can tell!
MID_EV14_017_m01_016: <ACA>Ugh, the taste of defeat makes me want to gag. You\nreally are a terrifying opponent, Leilidahna.
MID_EV14_017_m01_017: Well, I have no other choice, then. I must follow you\nlike a shadow until, at last, I can outmatch you!
MID_EV14_017_m01_018: That's right. I will not allow you to get away again!\nAnd when I do finally beat you...
MID_EV14_017_m01_019: I shall consider letting you admire me like you would\na big sister. Ohohoho!
MID_EV14_017_m01_020: What?! No! You are not following me around. You\ndon't know the meaning of the words "lay low"!
MID_EV14_017_m01_021: If I'm being honest, I find this woman to be more\nthan a little bit insufferable.
MID_EV14_017_m01_022: I think it is a fine idea. Olympia, you may do as\nyou please.
MID_EV14_017_m01_023: Oh, and Leilidahna, I have just recalled something\nof importance...
MID_EV14_017_m01_024: I believe the man you're searching for—Bertrand—\nmay still be alive.
MID_EV14_017_m01_025: What? Bertrand...is alive?
MID_EV14_017_m01_026: Please, Kalla, is that...is that true?!
MID_EV14_017_m01_027: As I recall, a prisoner was transferred from the\nkingdom of Arago to Dagsion at Mars's request.
MID_EV14_017_m01_028: This prisoner was sentenced to the Trial of the\nChariot. I believe his name was Bertrand.
MID_EV14_017_m01_029: The Trial has yet to be completed, and the man\nstill lives.
MID_EV14_017_m01_030: He's popular with the citizens of Dagsion. I hear\nthey call him the White-Maned Demon.
MID_EV14_017_m01_031: The White-Maned Demon... He's...alive!
MID_EV14_017_m01_032: I will kill him. With my own two hands. I will end\nhis life. I do not care what it takes.
MID_EV14_017_m01_033: I have to get to him before he finishes the Trial and\nleaves...or before someone else kills him!
MID_EV14_017_m01_034: I can tell there's no point in trying to stop you.
MID_EV14_017_m01_035: So be it. Soon they will hold the Heroic Games\nin Dagsion.
MID_EV14_017_m01_036: I heard rumors about it during my travels...though\nI'm unsure what it is precisely.
MID_EV14_017_m01_037: Mighty warriors from all over Dagda will gather, and\ndivine battles will be waged...
MID_EV14_017_m01_038: It's an offering meant to awaken our father, the\nDivine Emperor Dagda.
MID_EV14_017_m01_039: Though I have no idea what my brother is thinking.\nReviving our father will bring nothing but chaos.
MID_EV14_017_m01_040: But the Divine Sovereign has declared that he will\ngrant whatever wish the winner desires.
MID_EV14_017_m01_041: So if I win, and I wish for a battle with the\nWhite-Maned Demon...
MID_EV14_017_m01_042: He will grant your request, of course. For all of my\nbrother's faults, he is an honorable man.
MID_EV14_017_m01_043: This may work well for us, Miss Leda. If we go to\na crowded place like Dagsion...
MID_EV14_017_m01_044: we can gather details about Lechner's whereabouts.\nAnd of course, Bertrand will be in the arena.
MID_EV14_017_m01_045: If it pleases you, Kalla, I would like to go to\nDagsion at once.
MID_EV14_017_m01_046: You have made up your mind, I see. Very well, then.
MID_EV14_017_m01_047: My temple will arrange for you to take part in the\nHeroic Games. But please, rest here for now.